{
  "paraphrase": "For every subset H of Euclidean space ℝ⁴, where H consists of all points P such that the absolute value of each coordinate of P is at most 1/2, the operation 'contains' is defined as follows: For any real number r, 'contains r' holds if and only if there exists an affine subspace A of dimension 2 within ℝ⁴ and a point C in A such that the sphere of radius r centered at C intersects A and is entirely contained within H. Furthermore, this operation 'contains' is the greatest such operation that satisfies the given conditions."
}
